{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:32:03.294Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented task 4 in `openspec/changes/129-default-branch-steering/tasks/4.md`.\n\n**Source changes:**\n\n- `src/cli/plan-steer.ts`: `readSteeringPlan` now resolves changes through `findSteeringChange`, so an archived change in a worktree that needs steering is planned in place. Added default-branch awareness: for a `requirement_changed` trigger it emits `#### <capability>: <requirement> on <default branch>` with the requirement's text from the default branch (or `Removed on <default branch>.`), using `readRequirementsBase`, `changedRequirements`, `livingSpecPath`, and `parseCapabilitySpec`. When any trigger is a default-branch trigger it adds the restart or merge line after the tree line, and a `conflict` trigger replaces the done-tasks line with the restart wording.\n- `src/cli/lint.ts`: `resolveLintFolder` now tries `findSteeringChange` first, then falls back to `findSpecFolder`.\n- `src/cli/plan.ts`: no change needed — the existing steering path already writes `plan-prompt.md` into `folderPath` and starts sessions at `tree.root`.\n\n**Tests:** new `tests/steering-plan-default-branch.test.ts` with a self-contained temp git-repo setup covering the archived land-conflict prompt, the changed-requirement prompt text, and linting an archived steered change.\n\n**Verification:** the task verify and the proposal's `pnpm verify` both pass.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/129-default-branch-steering/.run/results/4.md`."}}
